# Cline Project Rules

## End-of-Session Git Push

- **ALWAYS** push all work to GitHub before ending a session.
- Before completing a task, run `git add -A && git status` to check for uncommitted changes.
- If there are uncommitted changes, commit them with a descriptive message.
- After committing, always run `git push origin <current-branch>` to push to GitHub.
- Verify the push succeeded before reporting task completion.
- This rule applies even if the task itself is not git-related — all accumulated work must be pushed.